$\begin{align}
9\cdot 9^2&=9^1\cdot 9^2
\\\\
&=9^{1+2}
\\\\
&=9^{3}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $x^m\cdot x^n=x^{m+n}$. Note that the powers have the same base.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
9\cdot 9^2&=\underbrace{9}_\text{1 time}\cdot\underbrace{9\cdot 9}_\text{2 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{9\cdot 9\cdot 9}_\text{3 times}
\\\\
&=9^{3}
\end{align}$
